# NorthNarrow COMBAT management carve-out (Beta Step 4b).
#
# Each line is an IPv4 or IPv6 address or CIDR allowed THROUGH during
# COMBAT isolation, so a remote operator on a declared management network
# keeps an SSH path and is not locked out when the host isolates. The agent
# reads this file at every COMBAT engage (never cached).
#
# The agent loads it only when an admin key with the `config-manage` role
# signed its exact content (external audit ATP-001): store it with
# `nn-admin config overlay set` (see docs/operator/COMBAT_RECOVERY.md) —
# a hand edit from a console is refused at the next engage.
#
# Format: one address (1.2.3.4, 2001:db8::1) or CIDR (1.2.3.0/24,
# 2001:db8::/48) per line. `#` starts a comment; blank lines are ignored.
# Each entry is allowed BOTH inbound (-s) and outbound (-d): IPv4 entries
# by iptables, IPv6 entries by ip6tables (COMBAT isolates both families).
#
# DEFAULT = EMPTY = full isolation (no carve-out). This is the
# security-first default; only add a network you trust to reach this
# host during an active incident.
#
# Fail-secure: a malformed line is skipped (logged), never widened, and
# an unreadable file applies NO carve-out at all.
#
# See docs/operator/COMBAT_RECOVERY.md before editing.
#
# Example (commented out — uncomment + edit for your management net):
#10.0.0.0/24
#198.51.100.7
